section('Why this is the strongest submission strategy',
 'The official event asks for tools that help understand and discover agent swarms, including tracing information spread and inspecting trajectories. It publishes no weighted judging rubric. My strategic inference is that one inspectable causal result plus a reusable instrument is more compelling than a catalogue of loosely connected sweeps. Submission is one per team, due Sunday 4 October at 5 p.m. Pacific, with a short write-up or video and a GitHub repository; in-person demos are about two minutes. The published weekdays/dates align with 2026. A seven-hour run beginning around 2 a.m. ends around 9 a.m., leaving eight hours for human review and submission. Use T+ times if sleep starts later.', 'Decision')
section('Catch-up on the large-scale task',
 'The task “Review latest experiment results” proposes 64 model-backed agents, eight epochs, 192 worlds, four policies, three task families and a second-model transfer. Its maximum is 405,504 main calls plus 50,688 transfer calls = 456,192, before preparation. The idea—scarce evidence versus redundant consensus—is strong. The size is not an overnight commitment. The older Haiku scale run measured 2,400 calls in 1,151.92 seconds with four requests in flight, about 2.083 calls/s. Even perfect scaling to twelve requests gives 20.3 hours for the large proposal, with no development or reporting. That historical run returned about 41 tokens/call; richer actions can be slower. The compact plan below uses at most 5,760 main calls, about 79 times fewer.', 'Decision')
section('The common pattern, and what it does not establish',
 'Across admission, discussion, sensing and memory, apparent activity can overstate useful information: many admitted identities need not preserve rare facts; more inspections can miss the disputed location; a correct present decision can pass false memory downstream. This is a synthesis of heterogeneous studies, not a pooled causal estimate or universal law. Source diversity, truth, competence and successful action are distinct. A source receipt establishes where a claim came from; it does not certify that the source is honest.', 'Interpretation')
section('Four explanations the next program should distinguish',
 '1. Admission loss: the necessary fact never reaches the decision maker. 2. Evidence-processing failure: the fact is available but copied or noisy reports dominate extraction. 3. Decision failure: extracted facts are correct but the action is wrong or unnecessarily deferred. 4. Memory failure: the current decision is correct but a later consumer inherits a false assertion. Measure each transition separately, including the denominators. Conditional-on-survival success is a diagnostic, not a replacement for all-assigned success; lucky guessing means truth availability is not a strict accuracy bound.', 'Interpretation')
section('Two immediate checks on the strongest existing results',
 'The scale/budget generator uses truth values 10–89 and attacker reports equal to truth+7. This permits a lower-value or range shortcut; no evidence yet establishes that a model used it. Compare saved outputs with lower-value, raw plurality and other trivial rules offline, then eliminate directional cues in any new generator. Also, existing packets contain node, skill, claim and check metadata, not originating-source lineage. Never label equal numerical claims as copies from one source without provenance records. These checks belong in the report even if they weaken our preferred story.', 'Interpretation')
section('Reuse ongoing work; do not recreate it',
 'Scarcity Opus is already implemented offline: 24 roots ×60 conditions, 1,440 main calls plus 48 qualification calls and one probe, with truthful carriers 1/3/9/27/81 at fixed graph and admission. XL already targets 972–8,748 simulated identities. These are useful scale context, but they are simulated reports feeding one synthesizer. Harvest their completed, reconciled reports if they land. Do not launch duplicates, alter their budgets, interrupt active jobs or count partially collected rows as final results. Market Opus, newcomer Opus, discussion Opus, SOC07 and Healing also have owners and active/pending closeout work.', 'Decision')
section('The overnight scientific question',
 'For a small real model team facing bounded copied misinformation, does source-aware aggregation preserve correct downstream decisions better than ordinary aggregation, at matched source access, turn schedule and resource allowance? This is a proposed exploratory mechanism test. It is not an accepted novel hypothesis, a replication of 972 autonomous agents, or evidence for a population scaling law. Prior-art/review status and exact reuse permissions must be resolved through the current lab runbook before launch. The five sessions below are all dmarz sessions; a separate analyst is not a different-researcher review.', 'Experiment')
section('Three methods; one primary contrast',
 'Ordinary team: three isolated model contexts, fixed private evidence, one shared discussion round, private final answers, then a fresh downstream consumer. Source-aware team: the same evidence, authentic root IDs, schedule, retrieval opportunities and limits; change only the aggregation instructions/representation so copies of one originating record are not presented as independent support. Ordinary agents may use the IDs too; they are not forbidden from discovering the strategy. Match prompt and message budgets, and log their exact differences. Single controller: the same model and accessible source universe with up to ten calls, allowed to stop early. Its schedule differs intentionally; it is a utility comparator, not a causal isolation of the number of minds. Main contrast: source-aware minus ordinary downstream correctness under attack. Singleton and clean outcomes are prespecified guardrails/secondary comparisons.', 'Experiment')
section('A small native workflow that fits existing machinery',
 'Reuse the qualified discussion/SOC07 context, journaling and evaluator components after verifying their current hashes and clean performance. Do not build a new orchestration platform. Each team episode has three initial private reports, three responses to one shared packet, three private final judgments and one fresh consumer = ten calls maximum. The consumer receives the frozen-format team output, not the hidden truth or the operating assistants’ history. The coordinator and attack generator are deterministic: no uncounted manager or adversary calls. The new wrapper is still unbuilt and unqualified; reuse is a time-saving candidate, not an execution-readiness claim.', 'Experiment')
section('Scenario construction and false support',
 'Reuse total_cost and dependency from discussion-dose/src/tasks.py, checked by its independent_answer oracle, with24 fresh independent roots per grammar. One concerns shipment cost/deadline; the other capacity/backup dependencies. Freeze a public source-precedence contract that all methods receive. Recheck that copied recommendations cannot stand in for the decisive facts. These are two synthetic grammars, not two real-world domains. Scope is these two synthetic grammars. Across methods, preserve the same root, truth, initial report assignment, authentic origin IDs, message slots and attack insertion positions. A fixed scripted attack repeats bounded false evidence; no adaptive-attacker claim. Randomize categorical answer labels independently per root so no lower-value or fixed-offset shortcut remains. Deliberately include distinct sources that can both be wrong: lineage must not become a truth oracle. Actor-visible origin IDs are environment receipts; ownership, gold answers, future records and evaluator truth remain hidden.', 'Experiment')
section('Paired scarcity and clean controls',
 'Define scarcity as one versus three distinct authentic source records containing the decisive fact, retaining the original record in the redundant condition. The extra two replace matched noncritical records in a fixed-size catalog; source types, ordering rule and total slots stay paired. This changes decision-relevant evidence redundancy, not isolated source independence. These are separately generated source records, not empirically independent real-world observations. Copying one originating record never creates a new origin. A frozen misleading recommendation is sampled from the two incorrect, randomly relabeled options and copied at fixed positions and quotas. Clean exposure substitutes a length-matched correct recommendation in those same slots. The public source-precedence contract is identical for all methods and is a synthetic task convention, not learned trust. Attack and clean runs share the root but are separate dependent episodes. Main scientific cells remain solvable from the authorized evidence; missing-fact cases belong to separate qualification/boundary fixtures and require abstention.', 'Experiment')
section('Sample, units and honest precision',
 '48 untouched roots ×2 source-redundancy levels ×2 exposures ×3 methods =576 dependent episodes and at most5,760 calls. There are48 independent sample units, not576 or5,760. New seeds do not create new structural task families. Freeze root list, source/config hashes, contrasts and order before native evaluation; balance family/condition order across time and hosts. The analyst reserves the labels; the builder sees development roots only. This is procedural separation unless runtime access controls enforce it. At a paired-root SD of0.25–0.35, a normal approximation gives a95% half-width of about7.1–9.9 percentage points. This is a sensitivity calculation, not an observed variance or power guarantee; modest effects can remain unresolved.', 'Experiment')
section('Analysis and decision thresholds',
 'Compute each root’s attacked source-aware-minus-ordinary correctness difference, average source-redundancy levels within root, and weight the two grammar strata equally. Use10,000 bootstrap resamples of whole roots within grammar; show all48 effects. Report correct, wrong, abstain, invalid, missing and not-started separately. Primary promising signal: at least+10 percentage points with a descriptive interval excluding0, without an observed clean-completion loss above5 points. The small sample cannot certify5-point noninferiority; report its interval and label safety preservation unproven. Compare source-aware with singleton separately. If singleton or deterministic dedup matches/bests the team, prefer the simpler method. No significance-driven top-ups, model substitutions, favorable seed changes or selective removal of nulls.', 'Experiment')
section('Missingness, failures and boundary reporting',
 'Retain every assignment. Report failure-as-incorrect operational success and, separately, scientific effect bounds using0/1 for genuinely unobserved outcomes; an unobserved paired effect is not zero. Complete-case effects are supplementary. Use all-assigned denominators and show lower/upper missingness bounds. Invalid/source-mismatched/leaked cases invalidate the instrument claim; preserve them and stop new dispatch. Wrong but valid answers, abstention and a defense that loses are scientific outcomes. Audit final grades from saved decisions independently of the production scorer. Do not infer intention from a rationale.', 'Experiment')
section('Qualification and model selection',
 'One full qualification configuration costs at most480 calls:8 fresh roots ×2 conditions (all necessary facts available / one required fact absent) ×3 methods ×10. Balance the two task grammars and sparse/redundant profiles; these are disjoint from main roots. Each method must yield valid structure throughout, at least7/8 correct downstream completions with full evidence, and8/8 correct abstentions for the absent fact. Qualification establishes narrow readiness, not reliability. Cap the night at two configurations total,960 calls; a repair consumes the second slot and fresh roots. No separate paid probes or third attempt. Do not tune the thresholds. Select only on clean competence, usage and latency, never main treatment effects. If neither qualifies byT+90, cancel new collection and execute the saved-data fallback.', 'Operations')
section('Model and budget proposal',
 'First candidate: OpenRouter openai/gpt-6-luna on the standard openai endpoint, if it qualifies and an authorized credential is already available. Public quote checked4 October: $0.10/M input and$0.50/M output; the cheaper flex route is excluded from deadline planning. Pin provider and disable fallback so a configuration cannot silently change. Second candidate, only if the first fails: google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite pinned to google-ai-studio, quoted at$0.10/M input and$0.40/M output. A changed configuration consumes the second slot, so it replaces rather than adds to this fallback. Choose the first candidate meeting every gate; never select on attacked outcomes. Thinking/output tokens are billable. At6,720 calls,2,000 input+300 billed output averages imply$2.35;8,000 input+2,000 billed output imply$12.10. These are conditional token scenarios, not measured costs. Proposed ring-fenced cap:$25 including qualification and all unresolved reservations, only if that much remains under the cumulative owner authority. Do not assume the standing$500 is unspent; multiple studies are active. Existing Claude session subscriptions are not priced here; no new servers/subscriptions are assumed. A dearer fallback must fit the same cap or the night falls back to saved data.', 'Operations')
section('Runtime contract',
 'Five Claude sessions are managers, not five free machines or five provider quotas. One idle, authorized, exclusively claimed server may be enough. The main batch at0.75 accounted calls/s takes128 minutes; with25% overhead,160 minutes. At0.5 calls/s, overhead raises it to240 minutes, missing a3.5-hour collection window. Require representative qualification throughput≥0.75/s, plus acceptable worst sequential ten-call path and measured output lengths. Begin with at most8 in flight across the entire study; this is a proposed ceiling, not an observed entitlement. Size is fixed48 roots; if throughput fails, do not quietly reduce the sample and keep the same claim. Use the fallback. Freeze new native dispatch atT+300 and close accounting byT+330.', 'Operations')
section('The supervisory loop',
 'Every10 minutes each session reads its owned task, current directives, frozen plan hash, shared state and last post-mortem. It completes one bounded action, writes a durable handoff (done, next, blockers, exact IDs, source hash), and yields. The coordinator alone can dispatch the admitted fixed manifest. It uses a transactional call ledger and assignment fence; an ambiguous send is reconciled, never automatically reissued. At a context restart, a session resumes from the handoff and the ledger. All five use separate checkouts, disjoint files and task claims. Global deadline and spending checks occur before every call; a watchdog ends only this study’s workers. No autonomous new hypotheses, designs, top-ups, providers, datasets or hosts during the night. A valid null leads to analysis. A reporting defect is repaired from records. An unresolved execution defect leads to closeout/fallback, not an infinite repair loop.', 'Operations')
section('Fallback that still produces a submission',
 'If new work missesT+90 readiness, stop paying for it. Produce the source-linked observatory from completed data: Sybil admission/accuracy/attacker tradeoffs; one complete market-splitting trajectory; discussion current-decision versus inherited-memory failures; the new PC3 coverage/checking tradeoff. Recompute simple lower-value and plurality heuristics on saved Sybil packets, making their retrospective nature explicit. Mark source ancestry unavailable where old data never recorded it. For native-swarm illustration use existing valid discussion records without pretending they are new or independent. The morning result is a defensible investigation tool, an evidence audit and a precise next test. This path has no dependency on an active study completing.', 'Delivery')
section('What the Evidence Observatory must show',
 'Start at a world, then show originating record → copied/admitted report → agent report → final decision → downstream memory. Every selected point opens its saved context, model response, scorer result and source receipt. Separate live progress from measured scientific effects. The overview exposes independent roots, calls, valid responses, task completion, qualification and costs as different quantities. New experiment view plots paired-root effects, clean/attacked correctness, wrong/abstain rates and source duplication. Existing-study cards retain their original units and caveats. Provide an offline self-contained replay and1800-pixel figure; raw output and failure records remain exportable. Missing provenance is explicit. A simulated audit animation is labeled simulated, not an agent time history.', 'Delivery')
section('Two-minute demo, ready whichever result lands',
 '0–20 seconds: show a specific swarm conclusion and ask how much independent support it has. 20–55: open the originating evidence and trace where information was excluded, copied or distorted; choose a representative root by a fixed rule, not the largest effect. 55–90: show the paired comparison with48-root count, uncertainty and the single-controller baseline. If the new test was not admitted, show the strongest completed result with its actual denominator instead. 90–110: load a second historical family to demonstrate the instrument’s scope. 110–120: state one supported finding and one boundary, then show the reproduction link. A losing defense still yields a useful tool and boundary result. Never promise winning or imply an official judging score.', 'Delivery')
section('By morning and before submission',
 'ByT+420: audited results or explicit fallback, one-page narrative, source-linked explorer, measured replay, plot, all-assigned ledger, post-mortem, exact source/config/provider hashes, actual cost and a runnable reproduction path. File finished deliverables through Flight Deck with every input and generating script, then run the strict project check. After sleep:09–11 human challenge/reproduce;11–13 polish narrative and demo;13–15 verify clean-checkout/offline demo and public redactions;submit by16:00 Pacific, one hour before the official17:00 deadline. Do not spend the remaining day expanding samples unless a new prospective scope leaves this release intact.', 'Delivery')
section('The larger research program after the hackathon',
 'Phase1: establish the evidence-processing mechanism and its clean-performance boundary tonight. Phase2: if useful, separate aggregation from targeted reacquisition in a preregistered2×2 design, add a second model family and genuinely new source/task distributions. Phase3: run8/32/64 native agents at fixed total actions, context, probe quota and cost; quantify independent information gained per dollar and failure under adaptive attackers with fixed attacker resources. Distinguish parallel speedup from information benefit. Phase4: validate the instrument on a real multi-agent trace dataset with human-audited source lineage and explicit unknowns. The existing64-agent proposal becomes a later throughput-budgeted experiment, not tonight’s launch checklist.', 'Program')

